diff --git a/docs/extensions/v1.1.md b/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
index ff2ee1f7..863d9d82 100644
--- a/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
+++ b/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
@@ -4195,3 +4195,27 @@ SDKs: Rust `Handler::resolve_debug(&DebugResolve) -> Resolved` (`Unchanged`, `Co
 `Refuse`); Go `DebugResolver.ResolveDebug` (nil to launch unchanged, `ErrDebugCancelled`, any other
 error refuses; `req.Context` ends with `0 cancel`); C the `debug_resolve` handler (0, 1 with `out`,
 -1 with `why`, -2). `rhun-ext-check` asks every `resolve = yes` debugger once per template section.
+
+## Local audio (experimental preview build)
+
+`[needs] audio = yes` declares access to local audio devices and services. The permission is
+shown at installation and on the extension page. Adding it during an update triggers the
+existing wider-access review. Older hosts ignore the key; handle unavailable audio gracefully.
+
+macOS grants Core Audio output services and AudioIO shared memory without a microphone grant.
+Linux grants `/dev/snd`, the PulseAudio runtime directory and the user's PulseAudio cookie.
+Linux sound services can also expose recording: this is local audio-service authority, not a
+playback-only sandbox guarantee. Windows extensions currently run without an OS sandbox,
+as before this addition. Playback extensions should open playback streams only.
+
+## Paired picture keys (experimental preview build)
+
+`view-key-state` requires `views` and `view-keys`. On macOS, X11, Wayland and Windows it adds
+`0 view VIEW key-up MODS NAME` alongside the existing key event, and
+`0 view VIEW mods MODS` when modifiers change. Release names use the unshifted key name.
+Key repeats remain ordinary key events. Window activation sends the focused picture
+`focus 1` or `focus 0`. Clear held keys on focus loss and closure. Bound editor commands keep
+their keys. Older hosts do not negotiate this feature; short key pulses are a possible fallback.
+X11 requests detectable autorepeat for this client. If the server does not support it, the host
+does not negotiate `view-key-state`, so synthetic autorepeat releases cannot be mistaken for
+physical releases. Headless controls also accept `key-up COMBO` for protocol-level tests.
